Final scope: App focus/workspace automatic refresh and CoverPanel's automatic assets/cover read share
one background promise. Foreground actions reserve the existing active lock immediately, await already
accepted background reads and execute once. Additional background reads cannot be accepted while a
foreground action holds that lock. Only the automatic CoverPanel effect receives the restricted
readAutomatically(contentId) API; explicit refresh and all mutation run calls remain foreground.
Library epoch/content identity, dirty draft handling, BUSY reporting/recovery and native operation
queue remain enforced. Probe used synthetic focus events and trusted Chromium input in an isolated
Electron copy, not installed-app macOS activation or a real assistant/provider call.
No full verification, installer rebuild, installation, plugin edit or shared dist-desktop edit was performed.
